IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc22-organizations.l4 -- sections 620 to 625.1 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (Part XX: organizations; record of proceedings; pre-hearing conference). Part agent ccc22. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE (the text's own words bring the case within the rule); JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Tags in the comments: [M-a] a failed "if"/"where" or a flat negative counted as the text's no; [M-b] a prohibition or grant limited by its own wording counted as NOT the text's no (NOTHING);
-- [F:...] a fork line for NOTES.md (may-if, may-where, entitled, duty, unless). Section 2 terms and other parts' answers are INPUTS named for their section.

§ `Section 620 -- Appearance by attorney`

-- src:12893 | 620 Every organization against which an indictment is filed shall appear and plead by counsel or agent.
@ref s 620 (src:12893-12893)
GIVEN `s 2 organization: the accused is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an indictment is filed against it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 620 the organization must appear and plead by counsel or agent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 organization: the accused is one` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the accused is an organization is for s 2 "organization"
        IF `s 2 organization: the accused is one` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every organization against which an indictment is filed"
        IF `an indictment is filed against it` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against which an indictment is filed"

§ `Section 621 -- Notice to organization`

-- src:12895 | 621 (1) The clerk of the court or the prosecutor may, where an indictment is filed against an organization, cause a notice of the indictment to be served on the organization.
@ref s 621(1) (src:12895-12895)
GIVEN `the person is the clerk of the court or the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an indictment is filed against an organization` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 621(1) the clerk of the court or the prosecutor may cause a notice of the indictment to be served on the organization` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is the clerk of the court or the prosecutor` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The clerk of the court or the prosecutor may"
        IF `an indictment is filed against an organization` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an indictment is filed against an organization, cause a notice of the indictment to be served on the organization" [F:may-where] [M-a]

-- src:12897 | (2) A notice of an indictment referred to in subsection (1) shall set out the nature and purport of the indictment and advise that, unless the organization appears on the date set out in the notice or the date fixed under subsection 548(2.1), and enters a plea, a plea of not guilty will be entered for the accused by the court, and that the trial of the indictment will be proceeded with as though the organization had appeared and pleaded.
@ref s 621(2) (src:12897-12897)
GIVEN `the notice sets out the nature and purport of the indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice advises that, unless the organization appears on the date set out in the notice or the date fixed under subsection 548(2.1), and enters a plea, a plea of not guilty will be entered for the accused by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice advises that the trial of the indictment will be proceeded with as though the organization had appeared and pleaded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 621(2) the notice has the contents subsection (2) requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice sets out the nature and purport of the indictment` AND `the notice advises that, unless the organization appears on the date set out in the notice or the date fixed under subsection 548(2.1), and enters a plea, a plea of not guilty will be entered for the accused by the court` AND `the notice advises that the trial of the indictment will be proceeded with as though the organization had appeared and pleaded`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall set out the nature and purport of the indictment and advise that" [M-a] [F:duty]

§ `Section 622 -- Procedure on default of appearance`

-- src:12899 | 622 Where an organization does not appear in accordance with the notice referred to in section 621, the presiding judge may, on proof of service of the notice, order the clerk of the court to enter a plea of not guilty on behalf of the organization, and the plea has the same force and effect as if the organization had appeared by its counsel or agent and pleaded that plea.
@ref s 622 (src:12899-12899)
GIVEN `the organization does not appear in accordance with the notice referred to in section 621` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is proof of service of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 622 the presiding judge may order the clerk of the court to enter a plea of not guilty on behalf of the organization` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the organization does not appear in accordance with the notice referred to in section 621` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an organization does not appear in accordance with the notice referred to in section 621, the presiding judge may" [F:may-where] [M-a]
        IF NOT `there is proof of service of the notice` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on proof of service of the notice"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12899 | 622 Where an organization does not appear in accordance with the notice referred to in section 621, the presiding judge may, on proof of service of the notice, order the clerk of the court to enter a plea of not guilty on behalf of the organization, and the plea has the same force and effect as if the organization had appeared by its counsel or agent and pleaded that plea.
@ref s 622 (src:12899-12899)
GIVEN `the plea of not guilty was entered on behalf of the organization by order under section 622` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 622 the plea has the same force and effect as if the organization had appeared by its counsel or agent and pleaded that plea` MEANS
    IF `the plea of not guilty was entered on behalf of the organization by order under section 622`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the plea has the same force and effect as if the organization had appeared by its counsel or agent and pleaded that plea"

§ `Section 623 -- Trial of organization`

-- src:12901 | 623 Where an organization appears and pleads to an indictment or a plea of not guilty is entered by order of the court under section 622, the court shall proceed with the trial of the indictment and, where the organization is convicted, section 735 applies.
@ref s 623 (src:12901-12901)
GIVEN `the organization appears and pleads to an indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a plea of not guilty is entered by order of the court under section 622` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 623 the court must proceed with the trial of the indictment` MEANS
    IF `the organization appears and pleads to an indictment` OR `a plea of not guilty is entered by order of the court under section 622`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an organization appears and pleads to an indictment or a plea of not guilty is entered by order of the court under section 622, the court shall proceed with the trial of the indictment" [M-a] [F:duty]

-- src:12901 | 623 Where an organization appears and pleads to an indictment or a plea of not guilty is entered by order of the court under section 622, the court shall proceed with the trial of the indictment and, where the organization is convicted, section 735 applies.
@ref s 623 (src:12901-12901)
GIVEN `the organization appears and pleads to an indictment, or a plea of not guilty is entered by order of the court under section 622` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the organization is convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 623 section 735 applies` MEANS
    IF `the organization appears and pleads to an indictment, or a plea of not guilty is entered by order of the court under section 622` AND `the organization is convicted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the organization is convicted, section 735 applies" [M-a]

§ `Section 624 -- Record of proceedings`

-- src:12905 | 624 (1) It is sufficient, in making up the record of a conviction or acquittal on an indictment, to copy the indictment and the plea that was pleaded, without a formal caption or heading.
@ref s 624(1) (src:12905-12905)
GIVEN `the record of a conviction or acquittal on an indictment copies the indictment and the plea that was pleaded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 624(1) the record of a conviction or acquittal on an indictment is sufficient without a formal caption or heading` MEANS
    IF `the record of a conviction or acquittal on an indictment copies the indictment and the plea that was pleaded`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is sufficient, in making up the record of a conviction or acquittal on an indictment, to copy the indictment and the plea that was pleaded, without a formal caption or heading"

-- src:12907 | (2) The court shall keep a record of every arraignment and of proceedings subsequent to arraignment.
@ref s 624(2) (src:12907-12907)
GIVEN `the proceeding is an arraignment or a proceeding subsequent to arraignment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 624(2) the court must keep a record of the proceeding` MEANS
    IF `the proceeding is an arraignment or a proceeding subsequent to arraignment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "of every arraignment and of proceedings subsequent to arraignment"

-- src:12909 | 625 Where it is necessary to draw up a formal record in proceedings in which the indictment has been amended, the record shall be drawn up in the form in which the indictment remained after the amendment, without reference to the fact that the indictment was amended.
@ref s 625 (src:12909-12909)
GIVEN `it is necessary to draw up a formal record in proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the indictment has been amended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 625 the record must be drawn up in the form in which the indictment remained after the amendment, without reference to the amendment` MEANS
    IF `it is necessary to draw up a formal record in proceedings` AND `the indictment has been amended`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where it is necessary to draw up a formal record in proceedings in which the indictment has been amended, the record shall be drawn up in the form in which the indictment remained after the amendment" [M-a] [F:duty]

§ `Section 625.1 -- Pre-hearing conference`

-- src:12913 | 625.1 (1) Subject to subsection (2), on application by the prosecutor or the accused or on its own motion, the court, or a judge of the court, before which, or the judge, provincial court judge or justice before whom, any proceedings are to be held may order that a conference between the prosecutor and the accused or counsel for the accused, to be presided over by the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice, be held prior to the proceedings to consider the matters that, to promote a fair and expeditious hearing, would be better decided before the start of the proceedings, and other similar matters, and to make arrangements for decisions on those matters.
@ref s 625.1(1) (src:12913-12913)
GIVEN `the application is made by the prosecutor or the accused, or the court acts on its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the court or a judge of the court before which, or the judge, provincial court judge or justice before whom, the proceedings are to be held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 625.1(1) the court may order a conference between the prosecutor and the accused or counsel for the accused before the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the application is made by the prosecutor or the accused, or the court acts on its own motion` AND `the person is the court or a judge of the court before which, or the judge, provincial court judge or justice before whom, the proceedings are to be held`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on application by the prosecutor or the accused or on its own motion, the court, or a judge of the court, before which, or the judge, provincial court judge or justice before whom, any proceedings are to be held may order"

-- src:12915 | (2) In any case to be tried with a jury, a judge of the court before which the accused is to be tried shall, before the trial, order that a conference between the prosecutor and the accused or counsel for the accused, to be presided over by a judge of that court, be held in accordance with the rules of court made under sections 482 and 482.1 to consider any matters that would promote a fair and expeditious trial.
@ref s 625.1(2) (src:12915-12915)
GIVEN `the case is to be tried with a jury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 625.1(2) a judge of the court must order a conference before the trial` MEANS
    IF `the case is to be tried with a jury`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any case to be tried with a jury"

-- src:12915 | (2) In any case to be tried with a jury, a judge of the court before which the accused is to be tried shall, before the trial, order that a conference between the prosecutor and the accused or counsel for the accused, to be presided over by a judge of that court, be held in accordance with the rules of court made under sections 482 and 482.1 to consider any matters that would promote a fair and expeditious trial.
@ref s 625.1(2) (src:12915-12915)
DECLARE `s 625.1(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 625.1(2) order that a conference between the prosecutor and the accused or counsel for the accused be held`

@ref s 625.1(2) (src:12915-12915)
GIVEN `the number of days from now until the trial begins` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 625.1(2) action`
`s 625.1(2) the judge must order the conference before the trial` MEANS
    PARTY `a judge`
    MUST `s 625.1(2) order that a conference between the prosecutor and the accused or counsel for the accused be held`
    WITHIN `the number of days from now until the trial begins`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "no order for a conference was made before the trial in a case to be tried with a jury"
